From 2f518b811f1804ed80efa8e485aa7690fd0e9f13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:55:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R1: restricted worker role for Fly Managed Postgres (on
 837aeb9)

- db-roles: a provider membership is tolerated only when named and proven
  read-only; effective DELETE/TRUNCATE/TRIGGER/REFERENCES is always a problem.
- apply-runtime-grants: RUNTIME_ROLE_READONLY_MEMBERSHIPS, RUNTIME_GRANTS_ALLOW_ABSENT
  (absent tables listed and skipped), RUNTIME_GRANTS_DRY_RUN (roll back).
- worker: WORKER_DATABASE_URL, role check before claiming
  (HUB_REQUIRE_RESTRICTED_DB_ROLE), WORKER_ONLY_RUN_ID, WORKER_EXIT_WHEN_RUN_DONE.
- create-run-main: one run, only for the approved input hash, only on an empty queue.
- r1-runtime-role.integration.test: production profile (0001-0007, Fly-shaped roles).

